DevOps Interview Preparation – Key Questions & Answers (EKS | AWS | Terraform | CI/CD)

Recently, while preparing for DevOps interviews, I compiled a set of real-world interview questions based on my hands-on experience. Sharing this in case it helps others preparing for Senior / 6+ years DevOps roles.

✅ How do you upgrade an EKS cluster?
Upgrade in phases:
Control plane first
Cluster add-ons (CNI, CoreDNS, kube-proxy)
Worker nodes using rolling or blue/green node groups
Ensures zero downtime and easy rollback.

✅ Why not in-place node upgrades?
Rolling upgrades with new node groups are safer and rollback-friendly.
🔹 Terraform & Infrastructure as Code

✅ Have you used Terraform modules?
Yes, created reusable modules and used for_each to provision tenant-specific resources dynamically.

✅ How do you handle rollback in Terraform?
Rollback is done by reverting the Git commit and re-running the pipeline. Terraform restores the previous desired state.

✅ GitHub Actions / Azure Pipelines
Used pipelines for:
Infrastructure provisioning
Application deployments
Scheduled automation (start/stop resources)
Choice depends on use case:
Lambda → event-based automation
Pipeline → controlled, auditable changes

✅ What is Warm Standby?
DR services run at minimal capacity and scale up quickly during a disaster.

✅ How is DB promoted during DR?
Read replicas are promoted to primary via automation or controlled pipelines after health checks.

✅ Why TLS inside Kubernetes?
Secures service-to-service communication, prevents MITM attacks, and meets compliance requirements.

✅ How do annotations work if they are read-only?
Annotations are metadata read by controllers (e.g., Prometheus) to take action like enabling metrics scraping.

